{"id":"2bacbc1cfb1a8f2d","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-cylinder.md","title":"Cylinder","display":"df-cylinder — Cylinder","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-cylinder","aliases":["58-df-cylinder","Cylinder"],"display":"df-cylinder — Cylinder","depends_on":["[[58-df-function]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-cylinder"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-cylinder</span><span>Cylinder</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-cylinder — Cylinder"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S,C\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3\">\\(S,C\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I\\subseteq\\mathbb R\">\\(I\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c\\in V\">\\(c\\in V\\)</span> (curve graph)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span> (line in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb R^3\">\\(\\mathbb R^3\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"v\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}\">\\(v\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\gamma\\in V\">\\(\\gamma\\in V\\)</span> (surface-parametrization graph)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> (set-coded function predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"58-df-function\">58-df-function</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ParallelVectorLine}_S(v,L)\">\\(\\operatorname{ParallelVectorLine}_S(v,L)\\)</span> (vector-line parallelism predicate defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CylinderSurface}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{CylinderSurface}_S\\)</span> (cylindrical-surface predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cylinder\\text{-}parallel}\\vdash \\operatorname{ParallelVectorLine}_S(v,L)\\leftrightarrow v\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\\exists p\\in\\mathbb R^3\\;\\left(L=\\{p+tv:t\\in\\mathbb R\\}\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cylinder\\text{-}parallel}\\vdash \\operatorname{ParallelVectorLine}_S(v,L)\\leftrightarrow v\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\\exists p\\in\\mathbb R^3\\;\\left(L=\\{p+tv:t\\in\\mathbb R\\}\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cylinder} \\vdash \\mathrm{CylinderSurface}_S(S,C,L,c,I,v)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(c,I,\\mathbb R^3)\\land C=\\operatorname{ran}(c)\\land\\operatorname{ParallelVectorLine}_S(v,L)\\land S=\\{c(s)+tv:s\\in I\\land t\\in\\mathbb R\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cylinder} \\vdash \\mathrm{CylinderSurface}_S(S,C,L,c,I,v)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(c,I,\\mathbb R^3)\\land C=\\operatorname{ran}(c)\\land\\operatorname{ParallelVectorLine}_S(v,L)\\land S=\\{c(s)+tv:s\\in I\\land t\\in\\mathbb R\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cylinder\\text{-}parametrization} \\vdash \\mathrm{CylinderSurface}_S(S,C,L,c,I,v)\\to\\exists\\gamma\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}(\\gamma,I\\times\\mathbb R,S)\\land\\forall s\\in I\\;\\forall t\\in\\mathbb R\\;(\\gamma(\\langle s,t\\rangle)=c(s)+tv)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cylinder\\text{-}parametrization} \\vdash \\mathrm{CylinderSurface}_S(S,C,L,c,I,v)\\to\\exists\\gamma\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}(\\gamma,I\\times\\mathbb R,S)\\land\\forall s\\in I\\;\\forall t\\in\\mathbb R\\;(\\gamma(\\langle s,t\\rangle)=c(s)+tv)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>This atom defines a cylindrical surface generated by translating a parametrized curve along a fixed nonzero direction.</li>\n<li>A volume formula belongs to a separately defined solid cylinder and requires planarity, perpendicular height, and measurability hypotheses; it is not a clause of this surface definition.</li>\n<li>No dependency on <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"873303ae0d44ae55\" href=\"?note=873303ae0d44ae55\" title=\"58-df-ruled\">58-df-ruled</a> is used here: that atom defines ruled algebraic varieties, not ruled surfaces in elementary differential geometry.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>do Carmo, Differential Geometry of Curves and Surfaces</li>\n<li>O'Neill, Elementary Differential Geometry</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-function","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}$ (set-coded function predicate, see [[58-df-function]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-ruled","status":"resolved","id":"873303ae0d44ae55","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Remark]","excerpt":"No dependency on [[58-df-ruled]] is used here: that atom defines ruled algebraic varieties, not ruled surfaces in elementary differential geometry.","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"S,C\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3","display":false},{"tex":"I\\subseteq\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"c\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb R^3","display":false},{"tex":"v\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\gamma\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ParallelVectorLine}_S(v,L)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CylinderSurface}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cylinder\\text{-}parallel}\\vdash \\operatorname{ParallelVectorLine}_S(v,L)\\leftrightarrow v\\in\\mathbb R^3\\setminus\\{0\\}\\land\\exists p\\in\\mathbb R^3\\;\\left(L=\\{p+tv:t\\in\\mathbb R\\}\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cylinder} \\vdash \\mathrm{CylinderSurface}_S(S,C,L,c,I,v)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Function}(c,I,\\mathbb R^3)\\land C=\\operatorname{ran}(c)\\land\\operatorname{ParallelVectorLine}_S(v,L)\\land S=\\{c(s)+tv:s\\in I\\land t\\in\\mathbb R\\}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}cylinder\\text{-}parametrization} \\vdash \\mathrm{CylinderSurface}_S(S,C,L,c,I,v)\\to\\exists\\gamma\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Function}(\\gamma,I\\times\\mathbb R,S)\\land\\forall s\\in I\\;\\forall t\\in\\mathbb R\\;(\\gamma(\\langle s,t\\rangle)=c(s)+tv)\\right)","display":true}],"bytes":2004,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-395","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-cylinder.md|58-df-cylinder]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["36d7463d215be751","873303ae0d44ae55"]}